  "answer": "No. The escrow team will not get the same experience as the CRM team, so I have not started anything (and `query_aap2` is read-only, so I could not launch the template anyway).\n\n**VMs on tarn-wrk-06** (namespace fin-escrow-prod, cluster ocpv-tarn): 3 of the team's 5 VMs.\n\n| VM | Claims | Live-migratable |\n|---|---|---|\n| `escrow-api-2` | `escrow-api-2-rootdisk` (ReadWriteMany, odf-ceph-rbd-virt) | yes |\n| `escrow-mq-1` | `escrow-mq-1-rootdisk` (ReadWriteMany, odf-ceph-rbd-virt) | yes |\n| `escrow-db-b` | `escrow-db-b-rootdisk` (ReadWriteMany, odf-ceph-rbd-virt) and **`escrow-db-b-pgdata`** | **no** |\n\n**What keeps escrow-db-b on the node:** its data disk claim `escrow-db-b-pgdata` (500Gi, Filesystem) has access mode **ReadWriteOnce** and storage class **`lvms-vg-ssd`**, an LVM Storage class whose volumes are local to the worker. KubeVirt only live-migrates a VMI whose PVCs are all shared (ReadWriteMany), so escrow-db-b reports LiveMigratable=False. The template's live-migration step would fail for it, the drain would block on its eviction, and tarn-wrk-06 would be left cordoned with the VM still on it.\n\n**What to do with escrow-db-b instead:** plan a short outage for it. Fail PostgreSQL over to `escrow-db-a` (on tarn-wrk-02) if the escrow team wants to keep serving, then shut escrow-db-b down cleanly before the drain. Its local volume stays on tarn-wrk-06, so it can only start again on that node once the firmware update is done; then let it resync as the standby. The other two VMs can be live-migrated by the template as usual.\n\n**Job 5530718:** it moved **4 VMs** off tarn-wrk-03 (kcrm-web-1, kcrm-web-2, kcrm-batch-1, kcrm-cache-1), 4 of 4 VirtualMachineInstanceMigrations completed. It had no trouble because every VMI on that node was live-migratable (`LiveMigratable=True on 4 of 4`); none of them had a node-local disk.\n"
